    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407-a2">

                <pb facs="0515" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg435"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bardel to the
                            mayor of Bamberg.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commercial Agency of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bamberg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1902-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                                1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the course of last night the coat of arms of the United States of America was
                    defiled in a dastardly manner by being completely covered with human excrement.
                    Besides that infamy, one of the windows in my consulate was smashed by a stone
                    being thrown through it.</p>
                <p>I herewith take the liberty of submitting the report of these contemptible acts
                    to your serious attention, being fully convinced that you will leave nothing
                    undone to see this outrage committed against a friendly nation avenged by severe
                    punishment of the perpetrators. At any rate, I must insist on a vigorous
                    investigation of this, to me, very painful occurrence.</p>
                <p>Yours, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Bardel</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Commercial
                    Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
